/-!
# Irreducible extension consequences for B.5.1

The cohomology reduction proves that the actual nonsplitting quotient belongs
to the natural list or is the marked Sp4(2)' natural module. Its proof uses
checked cohomology calculations for every excluded row, including the genuine
triple-cover argument. `linearThree_eq_top` independently establishes G = L
from the actual L3(2) isomorphism and retained outer-extension alternative.

Final assembly still requires the natural Sp4(2)'–A6 action equivalence and
the fixed-space obstruction for the linear-two and G2 dual extensions. Those
are genuine remaining mathematical prerequisites, not hypotheses asserting
the desired list or splitting of the present module.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), B.5.1(2),(5),
printed pp.99 and 102–103; I.1.5–6, printed p.408, and I.2.3, printed p.413.
-/
